  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat is the price of a movie ticket on the last Friday? Colby's parents give him $155 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 1; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nWhat is the price of a movie ticket on the last Friday? Colby's parents give him $155 each month to spend at the movies.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Assuming Colby goes to the movies on each of the **five Fridays** in the month and spends his allowance equally:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n155 \\\\div 5 = 31\\n\\\\]\\n\\nTherefore, the movie ticket on the last Friday costs\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\boxed{\\\\$31}\\n\\\\...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Colby's parents give him $150 each month to spend at the movies.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Assuming Colby spends his monthly allowance equally over the five Fridays:\n\n\\[\n150 \\div 5 = 30\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the movie ticket on the last Friday costs\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$30}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $11, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since the last Friday is a Friday, the ticket costs the Friday price:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$11}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Tickets for movies on Fridays and Saturdays cost $10, while tickets on all other days cost $7.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The last Friday is a Friday, so the ticket costs:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the last Friday is a regular Friday, not a holiday or special event.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "A regular Friday ticket costs $10, so the price is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Colby buys his ticket at the standard box-office price.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Colby buys a standard-price ticket, and the last Friday is a regular Friday. Friday tickets cost $10.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$10}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How many additional movies can Colby see on the last Friday while staying within his monthly movie budget? By the way, here are some relevant details: A tub of popcorn costs $8, and a box of candy costs $2. Colby has already seen 5 movies on Fridays or Saturdays and 8 movies on other days during the month. Colby has already had 2 tubs of popcorn and 4 boxes of candy during the month, and he wants one tub of popcorn and one box of candy on the last Friday.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Calculate Colby’s spending so far:\n\n- Friday/Saturday tickets: \\(5 \\times \\$10 = \\$50\\)\n- Other-day tickets: \\(8 \\times \\$7 = \\$56\\)\n- Popcorn: \\(2 \\times \\$8 = \\$16\\)\n- Candy: \\(4 \\times \\$2 = \\$8\\)\n\nTotal spent:\n\n\\[\n50+56+16+8=\\$130\n\\]\n\nHe has:\n\n\\[\n150-130=\\$20\n\\]\n\nleft. On the last Friday, popcorn and candy cost:\n\n\\[\n8+2=\\$10\n\\]\n\nThis leaves:\n\n\\[\n20-10=\\$10\n\\]\n\nfor movie tickets. Since each Friday ticket costs \\$10:\n\n\\[\n10\\div 10=1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Colby can see\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{1\\text{ additional movie}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
